{"id": "EUVD-2026-105018", "enisaUuid": "cce67572-4568-37c6-b602-858b28585a25", "description": "filelock is a platform-independent file lock for Python. From 3.30.0 until 4.2.1, StrictSoftFileLock versions from 3.30.0 and SoftReadWriteLock versions from 4.0.0 can adopt a protocol directory created first by another local user in a shared parent directory, allowing that user to alter protocol state and admit concurrent holders. This issue is fixed in version 4.2.1.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T14:21:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T14:21:24", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://github.com/tox-dev/filelock/security/advisories/GHSA-9c4x-gm8v-wgc4", "https://github.com/tox-dev/filelock/pull/839", "https://github.com/tox-dev/filelock/commit/bfa066d65a1ba9106f86ee9d027f7588b9c77e03", "https://github.com/tox-dev/filelock/releases/tag/4.2.1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112911"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "93b1fa47-8f7c-31ba-8c4b-a4ad4db8e57e", "product": {"name": "filelock", "vendor": {"name": "tox-dev"}}, "product_version": "3.30.0, < 4.2.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a4cfdaa2-fd9d-31a2-95df-caf2f012727f", "vendor": {"name": "tox-dev"}}], "isExploited": false}